-- demand_model.lut: the demand of a run, built from the arguments `run` takes, with its defaults
-- declared and recorded.
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-15, by Claude Fable 5.1, an agent of the coordinating session, on the brief
-- record/IA/demand-2026-10-15/prompt.md. A model file (12.S23): `theDemand` is the first demand
-- of all (L5.19), an action nobody called, so every argument has a declared default, and the
-- demand records them all (L5.18, 12.S18). The host's run.py, which builds the same demand from
-- the command line, is a specimen of this file (L14.3).
-- 2026-10-15, by Claude Opus 5.5, an agent of the coordinating session, on record/IA/
-- layer-3-review-2026-10-15/prompt-fix-BCD.md (B19 of its summary-BCD.md): `lawDemand` and
-- `recorded` are demand.lth's definitions now, and `Demanding`, the theory they modelled, is gone.
-- 2026-10-16, by Claude Opus 5.5, an agent of the coordinating session, on record/IA/
-- code-follows-2026-10-16/prompt-modes.md: the modes of running as arguments with their defaults
-- (D-2026-10-16-d), and the provisionals run as assumed, none by default (D-2026-10-16-c).
-- 2026-10-26, by Claude Opus 5.5: the per-law cutoffs, none by default (D-2026-10-16-k item 20).

import "demand.lth" Demand Strategy ForwardOnDemand LawCutoff
import "certification.lth" Value
import "test.lth" Grade Sampled AssumedGrade

-- The arguments of `run` (12.S17, 12.S18, 12.S13), each with the default the host holds today,
-- named here as a default and not as a constant (L5.18, P11). [proposed] `Sampled` as the grade
-- accepted when none is named (run.py's `ACCEPT`: an assumed entry serves only a run that accepts
-- assumed, 6.S10); no provisional run as assumed (D-2026-10-16-c: each is named); no fuel bound
-- and no time limit (D-2026-10-16-d, item 21 (c); the 10,000,000 steps of before cut runs that
-- needed more, and `certify` keeps its own budget, 7.S8); forward on demand as the strategy
-- (8.S3; run.py's call by need is its specimen while plan.lth's `TheDefaultsAgree` holds); not
-- fresh; `main` as the entry; no hole set; not checked; nothing pinned; no decoration (the
-- identity, 8.S1); [bite B1] a confidence of 0.05 for sampled evidence, the spec's rule of three
-- (7.S11), and the capped sum as the composition of evidence (L10.8, D-2026-10-25-a).
theDemand (entry : String <- "main") (accepts : Grade <- Sampled) (assumes : List String <- nil)
          (fuel : Maybe Nat <- nothing) (timeLimit : Maybe Float64 <- nothing)
          (sets : List (String * Value) <- nil) (checked : Bool <- false) (pinned : Maybe String <- nothing)
          (strategy : Strategy <- ForwardOnDemand) (fresh : Bool <- false)
          (axioms : Grade <- AssumedGrade) (roots : List String <- ["FileSystemKeeps", "SystemDelivers"]) (combine : String <- "weakest")
          (bound : Float64 <- 1.0) (delta : ProbabilityLevel <- 0.05) (composition : String <- "cappedSumComposition")
          (cutoffs : List LawCutoff <- nil) : Demand :=
  { entry := entry, decoration := nothing, accepts := accepts, assumes := assumes, delta := delta, fuel := fuel,
    timeLimit := timeLimit, sets := sets, checked := checked, pinned := pinned, strategy := strategy, fresh := fresh,
    axioms := axioms, roots := roots, combine := combine, bound := bound, composition := composition, cutoffs := cutoffs }
